INSERT [dbo].[Webinar] ([idWebinar], [Description], [DescriptionLong], [ImageUrl], [SmallImageUrl], [Status], [Title], [Date], [LearnCaption], [LearnBody], [WhoAttend], [Duration], [RecordingUrl], [idPresenter], [AdditionalNotifications], [ceu], [DateCreated], [DateChanged], [ConnectionInfo]) VALUES (1200, N'<p>This series is designed for bankers who have a year or less experience 
in call report preparation experience as well as OTS bankers who 
recently converted to the call report.</p>', N'<p><span style="font-weight: bold;">This 4 part webinar series will be held on September 10, 17, 24, and October 1 from 2:30pm-4:30pm ET.</span><br></p><p>This four part webinar is designed for bankers who are new to call report preparation and also OTS bankers who recently began filing a Call Report.&nbsp; The series will cover recent changes to the Call Report, basic reporting requirements, schedules that can be prepared using the general ledger and investment reports, loan schedules, maturity and repricing, and risk based capital.&nbsp; There will be exercises designed to reinforce the classification of balance sheet and income statement items, as well as classification requirements for loans.<br></p>', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', 4, N'Bank Call Report Prep - Part Four', CAST(0x0000A0DD00DE7920 AS DateTime), N'Covered Topics:', N'<p>The first webinar will review the 2012 changes to the Call Report, which primarily affect the lending schedules.&nbsp; General reporting requirements will also be reviewed, including consolidation rules, filing deadlines, procedures, and call report resources.&nbsp; Finally, the income statement schedules, RI and RI-E, which can be prepared using the general ledger, will be covered.&nbsp; At the end of the session an exercise on the income statement classifications will be provided.</p><p>The second webinar will cover the reporting requirements for the balance sheet schedules that can be prepared using the bank’s general ledger and investment reports, including&nbsp; RC, RC-B, RC-E, RC-F, RC-G, RC-K, parts of RC-M, and RC-O.&nbsp; An exercise on the balance sheet and income statement schedules will be provided.</p><p>The third webinar will cover the loan classification requirements of RC-C, reporting of charge-offs and recoveries, past due loans, insider loans, and off balance sheet items.&nbsp; An exercise on loan coding will be provided.</p><p>The final webinar will cover interest rate risk reporting, risk based capital, and the remaining call report schedules, RC-Q, RC-S, RC-T, RC-U, and RC-V.&nbsp; There are proposed regulatory changes to the Risk Based Capital rules that, if approved, would likely affect the Call Report in 2015.&nbsp; A summary of the changes will be provided.<br></p>', N'<p>This series is designed for bankers who have a year or less experience in call report preparation experience as well as OTS bankers who recently converted to the call report.<br></p>', CAST(2.00 AS Decimal(18, 2)), N'CallRptPt41012.wmv', 10564, N'info@ttstrain.com', N'10 CRCM, 10 CSOP credits|The Institute of Certified Bankers (ICB) is dedicated to promoting the highest standards of performance and ethics within the financial services industry.&nbsp; Call Report Preparation for Beginners - Four Part Webinar has been approved for 10 CRCM, 10 CSOP credits.&nbsp; This statement should not be viewed as an endorsement of this program or its sponsor.', CAST(0x0000A092012555C0 AS DateTime), CAST(0x0000A09200D2A9B0 AS DateTime), NULL)
GO
INSERT [dbo].[Webinar] ([idWebinar], [Description], [DescriptionLong], [ImageUrl], [SmallImageUrl], [Status], [Title], [Date], [LearnCaption], [LearnBody], [WhoAttend], [Duration], [RecordingUrl], [idPresenter], [AdditionalNotifications], [ceu], [DateCreated], [DateChanged], [ConnectionInfo]) VALUES (1201, N'This program fulfills many of your annual training requirements for your frontline!', N'<p>This program fulfills many of your annual training requirements for your frontline!</p><p>The front-line is critical in the implementation of many of the federal regulations for a financial institution.&nbsp; In this program, we will cover the basic understanding of what each regulation is for and how the frontline is responsible for its implementation.&nbsp; Your staff will be updated and have a review of the new requirements for this year and some proposed changes.&nbsp; You will want to document this training for your examiners and count this to the job specific training for BSA as well as the other deposit regulations.</p>', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', 4, N'Deposit Compliance:  Frontline Deposit Regulations', CAST(0x0000A0F400A4CB80 AS DateTime), N'What You Will Learn:', N'<ul><li>Regulation D:&nbsp; DDA, NOW and FDIC requirements for insurance disclosures on DDAs with interest</li><li>Regulation D:&nbsp; Savings transaction limitations</li><li>Regulation CC:&nbsp; Holds and proposed changes on disclosures</li><li>Regulation E:&nbsp; ODP requirements and error resolution</li><li>BSA and the NEW CTR and its components</li><li>Red Flags for Identity theft</li><li>Regulation GG and unlawful internet gambling</li><li>BSA:&nbsp; Customer Identification Program and Customer Due Diligence</li><li>Regulation DD:&nbsp; Interest and APY calculations, disclosures to customers</li><li>And much much more</li></ul>', N'<p>Customer Service Representatives, Branch Administration, Personal Bankers, Branch Managers, Deposit Operations, Tellers, New Account Representatives.</p>', CAST(2.00 AS Decimal(18, 2)), N'DepositComplianceDC1012.wmv', 10568, N'info@ttstrain.com', N'|', CAST(0x0000A093010DFD30 AS DateTime), CAST(0x0000A09301118F40 AS DateTime), NULL)
GO
INSERT [dbo].[Webinar] ([idWebinar], [Description], [DescriptionLong], [ImageUrl], [SmallImageUrl], [Status], [Title], [Date], [LearnCaption], [LearnBody], [WhoAttend], [Duration], [RecordingUrl], [idPresenter], [AdditionalNotifications], [ceu], [DateCreated], [DateChanged], [ConnectionInfo]) VALUES (1202, N'<p>If you want to "jump start" your IRA knowledge base, this two hour Webinar is a good place to begin.</p>', N'<p>One of the most common questions you may get when a customer or member walks through the door is:&nbsp; "What kind of IRA plan should I open?" or "Which type of IRA is best for me?"&nbsp; We know that most of us are not in the position or licensed to give the potential IRA accountholder "advice".&nbsp; But, there is nothing wrong with explaining the different IRA products to them - if you know the facts.</p><p>If you want to "jump start" your IRA knowledge base, this two hour Webinar is a good place to begin.</p>', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', 4, N'IRA Plan Types - Simplified', CAST(0x0000A0EE00A4CB80 AS DateTime), N'Covered Topics:', N'<ul><li>Traditional IRAs - qualifications, contribution limits and distribution timing.</li><li>Roth IRAs - qualifications, contribution limits and tax free distributions</li><li>Conversion Roth IRAs - taxability and reporting as well as tax free distributions</li><li>Simplified Employee Pension Plans - qualifications and coding</li><li>Review of forms and IRS reporting for each plan type (You are encouraged to have a copy of your application and contribution form available for reference during the webinar).</li></ul>', N'<p>All entry and medium level customer service reps, as well as experienced supervisor who would like to review the latest IRA plan rules and regulations.</p>', CAST(2.00 AS Decimal(18, 2)), N'IRAPlanTypesTY1012.wmv', 28, N'info@ttstrain.com', N'| ', CAST(0x0000A099010F5CC0 AS DateTime), CAST(0x0000A0990110BC50 AS DateTime), NULL)
GO
INSERT [dbo].[Webinar] ([idWebinar], [Description], [DescriptionLong], [ImageUrl], [SmallImageUrl], [Status], [Title], [Date], [LearnCaption], [LearnBody], [WhoAttend], [Duration], [RecordingUrl], [idPresenter], [AdditionalNotifications], [ceu], [DateCreated], [DateChanged], [ConnectionInfo]) VALUES (1203, N'Answers the most frequently asked legal questions.', N'<p><i>Answers the Most Frequently Asked Legal Questions</i></p><p><b>Improve Your System:</b>&nbsp; Questions regarding the USA Patriot Act, Suspicious Activity Reports, Know Your Customer, power of attorneys, deceased renters, payable on death leases, living trusts, court orders, Americans with Disabilities Act, past due boxes, abandoned property and many other legal and compliance areas have caused great concern and confusion for the safe deposit industry. At this workshop you will receive current information about all of these issues and an in-depth explanation about how they impact on your financial institution and your safe deposit box renters.</p><p><b>David McGuinn</b>, a nationally known expert in the area of safe deposit, will provide clear concise answers to complicated questions regarding your institution''s responsibility and potential liability. He will also identify and discuss various compliance issues relating to each legal topic.</p>', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', 4, N'Safe Deposit Regulatory Compliance & Legal Issues', CAST(0x0000A0F500A4CB80 AS DateTime), N' What You Will Learn:', N'<p>Get answers to the following questions and establish internal procedures to comply with your own safe deposit requirements.</p><br><ul><li>What seven suspicious safe deposit transactions always trigger a SAR?</li><li>How does the USA Patriot Act affect all safe deposit areas nationwide?</li><li>What BSA &amp; SAR violations are compliance examiners finding today?</li><li>What should we do if dangerous content are found in a past due box?</li><li>When are box contents sent to the Unclaimed Property Department?</li><li>In most states who must be present when a past due box is drilled?</li><li>How can poor box drilling procedures make a box renter very rich?</li><li>Do you have "Right of Offset" against a past due renter''s account?</li><li>What past due fees can be collected from a delinquent box renter?</li><li>Can you report a past due box renter to a credit-reporting agency?</li><li>What careful wording should be used in a <u>FINAL</u> past due notice?</li><li>What amount of safe deposit liability insurance should you carry?</li><li>How does the American with Disabilities Act affect safe deposit?</li><li>Who can legally enter a deceased renter''s box in most states?</li><li>How should you answer a renter''s question about insurance?</li><li>Should a power of attorney be used to enter a renter''s box?</li><li>How can adding a "payable on death" clause get you sued?</li><li>Can money, guns or drugs be legally stored in a box?</li></ul>', N'<p>This informative program is designed to update safe deposit supervisors, vault attendants, cashiers, branch managers, compliance officers, auditors, training directors, new account personnel and your in-house legal counsel.</p>', CAST(2.00 AS Decimal(18, 2)), N'SafeDepCompCD1012.wmv', 10567, N'info@ttstrain.com', N'|', CAST(0x0000A09A009523B0 AS DateTime), CAST(0x0000A09A00AF3B60 AS DateTime), NULL)
GO
INSERT [dbo].[Webinar] ([idWebinar], [Description], [DescriptionLong], [ImageUrl], [SmallImageUrl], [Status], [Title], [Date], [LearnCaption], [LearnBody], [WhoAttend], [Duration], [RecordingUrl], [idPresenter], [AdditionalNotifications], [ceu], [DateCreated], [DateChanged], [ConnectionInfo]) VALUES (1204, N'Tips and training for compliance with the new rules.', N'<p><i>Tips and training for compliance with the new rules.</i></p><p>Our topic for the webinar will focus on the changes to Reg E that become effective <b>February 13, 2013.&nbsp; <i>Start planning now!</i></b>&nbsp; This change may present significant operational challenges to your institution.&nbsp; Here''s what the CFPB (Consumer Financial Protection Bureau) announced: </p><p>The Consumer Financial Protection Bureau (CFPB) adopted <u>a rule that will increase protections for consumers who transfer money internationally</u>.&nbsp; Under the new rule, remittance transfer providers will generally be required to disclose the exchange rate and all fees associated with a transfer so that consumers know exactly how much money will be received on the other end.&nbsp; The rule also requires remittance transfer providers to <u>investigate disputes and remedy errors</u>.</p><p>Does your institution accept foreign wire transfer instructions or ACH credit entries from consumers or allow consumers to send online bill payments to foreign addresses?&nbsp; Certain prepaid access card transactions may trigger these new Regulation E provisions.&nbsp; <b>WILL YOU BE PREPARED?</b>&nbsp; Listen to this session and learn about the new disclosures, definitions, and error resolution procedures that will be required.&nbsp; You will learn important tips to help you understand the answers to these questions and issues.</p>', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', 4, N'Reg E Remittance Transfers, Customer Disputes and Disclosures', CAST(0x0000A0D100A4CB80 AS DateTime), N'Covered Topics:', N'<ul><li>Is your financial institution a "<b>remittance transfer provider</b>"?</li><li>What does the "normal course of business" mean?&nbsp; Will you have to comply with these new requirements or will you be exempt?</li><li>What is a preauthorized remittance transfer?</li><li>What are the procedures for error resolution claims? Will this be a risk for increased fraud activity?</li><li>When are disclosures required? How can they be delivered? </li><li>We''ll review A-30 through A-41 model disclosures. What''s in the disclosure forms and what must be provided?</li><li>How are exchange rates, taxes and fees disclosed?</li><li>What happens when a request is made in advance?</li><li>How are cancellations for transfer requests handled?</li><li>The Consumer Financial Protection Bureau has proposed additional amendments to the definition of "remittance transfer provider", the use of estimates, and other considerations.</li></ul><p>You will receive summary materials discussing the regulation and the Bureau''s proposed amendments, plus copies of sample disclosures to help you comply with the new requirements of the regulation.</p>', N'<p>Customer Service Reps, New Account Reps, Deposit Operations staff including the ACH and Wire Transfer areas, Security and Compliance Officers will find this session very beneficial.</p>', CAST(2.00 AS Decimal(18, 2)), N'RegEEG0912.wmv', 14668, N'info@ttstrain.com', N'|', CAST(0x0000A09B00C88020 AS DateTime), CAST(0x0000A09B00CB8590 AS DateTime), NULL)
GO
INSERT [dbo].[Webinar] ([idWebinar], [Description], [DescriptionLong], [ImageUrl], [SmallImageUrl], [Status], [Title], [Date], [LearnCaption], [LearnBody], [WhoAttend], [Duration], [RecordingUrl], [idPresenter], [AdditionalNotifications], [ceu], [DateCreated], [DateChanged], [ConnectionInfo]) VALUES (1205, N'<p>Don''t miss this interactive webinar presented by a former examiner and an expert in the payments industry.</p>', N'<p>The Department of the Treasury Financial Crimes Enforcement Network (FinCEN) issued Advisory FIN-2012-A010 on October 22, 2012, Risk Associated with Third-Party Payment Processors.&nbsp; FinCEN issued the advisory due to reports of recent increases in certain criminal activity by Payment Processors, which presents a risk to the payment systems by making them vulnerable to money laundering, identity theft, fraud schemes, and illicit transactions. The advisory also discusses the potential requirements for filing Suspicious Activity Reports (SARs).<br></p><p>Developing a relationship with a third-party processor can be extremely valuable and a very positive experience.&nbsp; However, there are additional rules and compliance steps that must be followed when building this relationship and in the procedures and processes you must have in place when working with a third-party processor.&nbsp; This webinar will examine these rules and compliance challenges.&nbsp; We''ll examine how a third party processor affects your ability to process transactions and affects your ability to remain in compliance with the rules and regulations that govern ACH.&nbsp; You''ll also discuss what IT security examiners are concerned with and what they may be looking for when doing an audit.</p><p>Don''t miss this interactive webinar presented by a former examiner and an expert in the payments industry.<br></p>', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', 4, N'Third Party Payment Processors - Why are Examiners Concerned?', CAST(0x0000A10200DE7920 AS DateTime), N'Covered Topics:', N'<ul><li>Develop an understanding of the role a third-party processor plays in ACH</li><li>Examine the ACH Operating Rules surrounding third-party processors</li><li>Gain insight into the concerns of financial institution IT security examiners</li><li>Discuss the new FDIC guidance that relates to third-party processors</li></ul>', N'<p>ACH Operations, Compliance, Risk Managers, Operations, Senior Management, and Auditors.</p>', CAST(2.00 AS Decimal(18, 2)), N'TPPPKW1112.wmv', 10607, N'info@ttstrain.com', N'|', CAST(0x0000A0A2009A5BA0 AS DateTime), CAST(0x0000A0A2009C8E20 AS DateTime), NULL)
GO
INSERT [dbo].[Webinar] ([idWebinar], [Description], [DescriptionLong], [ImageUrl], [SmallImageUrl], [Status], [Title], [Date], [LearnCaption], [LearnBody], [WhoAttend], [Duration], [RecordingUrl], [idPresenter], [AdditionalNotifications], [ceu], [DateCreated], [DateChanged], [ConnectionInfo]) VALUES (1206, N'<p>Twenty steps to stellar professional development results.</p>', N'<p><b>This is part one of a two-part series.&nbsp; Part two is being held on September 14<sup>th</sup>.&nbsp; <a href="http://www.bankwebinars.com/Webinar/Details/1207">Click here for more information on part two</a>.</b><br></p><p><i>Twenty Steps to Stellar Professional Development Results</i></p><p>When it comes to training, set your sights on your destination, map out the route and pay the toll.&nbsp; Clear a path for training to become a rock solid contributor to your culture, efficiencies and bottom line. </p><p>Everyone invested in your financial institution hopes that the staff - from top to bottom - is well-trained.&nbsp; Are you using hope and luck as your strategies for making training a priority or do you enjoy the comfort that comes with needs assessment, goals and a plan?&nbsp; I am sure you would agree you need to rely on more than hope when it comes to people knowing how to do their job so that the company can build a well-earned reputation for excellence among clients, regulators, peer, investors and the community.</p><p>Training is about preventing problems, solving problems, enhancing confidence and building collective and individual intelligence.</p><p>It''s interesting that there is a mandate for a financial institution to have a disaster recovery plan but not a plan for training and developing the staff.&nbsp; Maybe now is the time to issue that mandate and ensure training and professional development become a top priority at your company.&nbsp; How do you do that?<br></p>', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', 4, N'Navigating the Training Process - Part One', CAST(0x0000A0C500A4CB80 AS DateTime), N'Part One - Finding Answers to Tough Questions:', N'<blockquote><ol><li>What is the track record of training?</li><li>Is learning a part of the culture?</li><li>Who should own training?</li><li>Who is responsible for training success?</li><li>How many dollars does it take?</li><li>How do you know who needs what?</li><li>How do you put a stop to defending, complaining and blaming??</li><li>What are the potential derailments training faces?</li><li>How do you keep training effective, on target and current?</li><li>How do you organize and monitor training?</li></ol></blockquote>', N'<p>Training directors, their assistants, human resource personnel, and 
others who want to learn how to better assess training needs, produce 
cost effective materials, and develop targeted programs that meet -- 
even exceed -- the organization''s goals.  </p>', CAST(2.00 AS Decimal(18, 2)), N'NavTraining1TN0912.wmv', 25, N'info@ttstrain.com', N'| ', CAST(0x0000A0A7010F5CC0 AS DateTime), CAST(0x0000A0A70112EED0 AS DateTime), NULL)
GO
INSERT [dbo].[Webinar] ([idWebinar], [Description], [DescriptionLong], [ImageUrl], [SmallImageUrl], [Status], [Title], [Date], [LearnCaption], [LearnBody], [WhoAttend], [Duration], [RecordingUrl], [idPresenter], [AdditionalNotifications], [ceu], [DateCreated], [DateChanged], [ConnectionInfo]) VALUES (1207, N'<p>Twenty steps to stellar professional development results.</p>', N'<p><b>This is part two of a two-part series.&nbsp; Part one is being held on September 7<sup>th</sup>.&nbsp; <a href="http://www.bankwebinars.com/Webinar/Details/1206">Click here for more information on part one</a>.</b><br></p><p><i>Twenty Steps to Stellar Professional Development Results</i></p><p>When it comes to training, set your sights on your destination, map out the route and pay the toll.&nbsp; Clear a path for training to become a rock solid contributor to your culture, efficiencies and bottom line. </p><p>Everyone invested in your financial institution hopes that the staff - from top to bottom - is well-trained.&nbsp; Are you using hope and luck as your strategies for making training a priority or do you enjoy the comfort that comes with needs assessment, goals and a plan?&nbsp; I am sure you would agree you need to rely on more than hope when it comes to people knowing how to do their job so that the company can build a well-earned reputation for excellence among clients, regulators, peer, investors and the community.</p><p>Training is about preventing problems, solving problems, enhancing confidence and building collective and individual intelligence.</p><p>It''s interesting that there is a mandate for a financial institution to have a disaster recovery plan but not a plan for training and developing the staff.&nbsp; Maybe now is the time to issue that mandate and ensure training and professional development become a top priority at your company.&nbsp; How do you do that?<br></p>', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', 4, N'Navigating the Training Process - Part Two', CAST(0x0000A0CC00A4CB80 AS DateTime), N'Part Two - Ensuring Training Sticks:', N'<blockquote><ol><li>Establishing training standards</li><li>Creating value and interest</li><li>Identifying resources - who trains on what, delivery options</li><li>Clarifying the needs of the trainer</li><li>Building key partnerships</li><li>Specifying training objectives</li><li>Designing training that sticks</li><li>Presenting training tips </li><li>Managing headaches, disappointment and challenges </li><li>Training follow-up</li></ol></blockquote>', N'<p>Training directors, their assistants, human resource personnel, and 
others who want to learn how to better assess training needs, produce 
cost effective materials, and develop targeted programs that meet -- 
even exceed -- the organization''s goals.  </p>', CAST(2.00 AS Decimal(18, 2)), N'NavTraining2RT0912.wmv', 25, N'info@ttstrain.com', N'| ', CAST(0x0000A0A7011567A0 AS DateTime), CAST(0x0000A0A70115F440 AS DateTime), NULL)
GO
INSERT [dbo].[Webinar] ([idWebinar], [Description], [DescriptionLong], [ImageUrl], [SmallImageUrl], [Status], [Title], [Date], [LearnCaption], [LearnBody], [WhoAttend], [Duration], [RecordingUrl], [idPresenter], [AdditionalNotifications], [ceu], [DateCreated], [DateChanged], [ConnectionInfo]) VALUES (1208, N'<p>This webinar will offer tips on what to do to avoid the traps and in so 
doing help make frontline staff more efficient, confident and prepared 
to tackle the daily responsibility of being on the frontline.</p>', N'<p>The frontline staff at any financial institution holds the keys to the success of that organization. Therefore, the goal of every financial institution is to develop their frontline staff into successful independent contributors, as well as valuable team players. The <i>Ten Traps to Avoid on the Frontline</i> webinar takes a look at those behaviors, thoughts and attitudes that frontline staff can fall into without realizing the negative impact that can be made on customers, management and the financial institution.</p><p>Whether frontline staff is new or long-term, there is an opportunity during this webinar to learn, or to be reminded of the traps that can bankrupt their success or lead to a miscarriage of any institution''s mission to serve its customers well.&nbsp; This webinar will offer tips on what to do to avoid the traps and in so doing help make frontline staff more efficient, confident and prepared to tackle the daily responsibility of being on the frontline.</p>', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', 4, N'Ten Traps to Avoid on the Frontline', CAST(0x0000A0EC00DE7920 AS DateTime), N'Frontline Staff Want to Avoid These Traps:', N'<blockquote><ol><li>Ignoring Reputation Destroyers &nbsp;</li><li>Relying on a Single Skill-Set </li><li>Deferring to Someone Else to Solve Issues</li><li>Slipping into Unprofessional Behavior </li><li>Resistance to Double-Checking Work and Decisions</li><li>Failing to Correct Critical Thinking Errors</li><li>Teamwork Hiccups </li><li>Being Too Rigid or Too Lax</li><li>Buying into Prejudice or Stereotyping</li><li>Blind Spots when it comes to Customer Service</li></ol></blockquote>', N'<p>All Frontline Staff including Tellers, Head Tellers, Teller Supervisors, News Accounts, Loan Preparers and Trainers would all benefit from this webinar.</p>', CAST(2.00 AS Decimal(18, 2)), N'TenTrapsTT1012.wmv', 10578, N'admin@ttstrain.com, info@ttstrain.com', N'|', CAST(0x0000A0AE01126230 AS DateTime), CAST(0x0000A0D800E4CA50 AS DateTime), NULL)
GO
INSERT [dbo].[Webinar] ([idWebinar], [Description], [DescriptionLong], [ImageUrl], [SmallImageUrl], [Status], [Title], [Date], [LearnCaption], [LearnBody], [WhoAttend], [Duration], [RecordingUrl], [idPresenter], [AdditionalNotifications], [ceu], [DateCreated], [DateChanged], [ConnectionInfo]) VALUES (1209, N'<p>Be ready for both the compliance and operational changes, so that your escrows meet all the requirements.</p>', N'<p>Reg. Z rules require that certain loans, known as Higher-Priced Mortgage Loans (HPML),maintain escrow accounts for taxes and insurance for at least the first year. Many banks have only just started the escrow process, and although you might not want to start now, Dodd-Frank requirements will only broaden the scope of the requirement. The writing is on the wall: eventually all consumer mortgage loans will likely require escrows.</p><p>This webinar will provide you with the requirements under both Reg. Z and RESPA (since HPMLs are also covered by RESPA, you''ll have to comply with that rule''s escrow provisions, as well). We''ll also talk about the CFPB''s new disclosure requirements and where escrow information will appear on the new forms.</p><p>Be ready for both the compliance and operational changes, so that your escrows meet all the requirements.</p>', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', 4, N'Dealing with Escrows, including Coming Changes', CAST(0x0000A0D000A4CB80 AS DateTime), N'Covered Topics:', N'<ul><li>What loans require escrows under the new Reg. Z HPML rule</li><li>Coming requirements under Dodd-Frank to further expand escrow requirements for more loans</li><li>RESPA''s escrow requirements, including disclosures and accounting rules</li><li>Figuring how to complete the escrow lines on the existing GFE and HUD-1 </li><li>How escrows will be disclosed on new mortgage forms: the Loan Estimate and Closing Disclosure</li><li>Utilizing the aggregate accounting method</li><li>Initial, annual, and short-year account statements</li><li>Dealing with surpluses, shortages, and deficiencies</li><li>What to do about payment shock</li></ul>', N'<p>Mortgage lenders, originators, compliance professionals, auditors, senior management, and anyone else involved in the mortgage or escrow process will be particularly interested in this webinar''s material.</p>', CAST(2.00 AS Decimal(18, 2)), N'EscrowsWS0912.wmv', 24, N'info@ttstrain.com, dparker@bomwv.com', N'|', CAST(0x0000A0B000B42D00 AS DateTime), CAST(0x0000A0B000BD83A0 AS DateTime), NULL)
GO
INSERT [dbo].[Webinar] ([idWebinar], [Description], [DescriptionLong], [ImageUrl], [SmallImageUrl], [Status], [Title], [Date], [LearnCaption], [LearnBody], [WhoAttend], [Duration], [RecordingUrl], [idPresenter], [AdditionalNotifications], [ceu], [DateCreated], [DateChanged], [ConnectionInfo]) VALUES (1210, N'<p>We will review Federal requirements of the NEW E-OSCAR, and using&nbsp; METRO-2 format when reporting.</p>', N'<p>Whether you report to one or all four of the National Credit Reporting Agencies (CRA), you are required to comply with the Fair Credit Reporting Act and the Fair and Accurate Credit Transaction Act (FACTA) amendment. It''s not what you know that will hurt you-it''s re-polluting the consumer''s file that can cost your Financial Institution plenty! We will review Federal requirements of the NEW E-OSCAR, and using&nbsp; METRO-2 format when reporting. We will also discuss the pros and cons of reporting to more than one NCRA (National Credit Reporting Agency), and why you are required to run quality control checks on your data to make sure it is correct, and you are in compliance.</p>', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', 4, N'Reporting Your Credit Data, E-OSCAR, METRO 2 & FACTA Compliance & Audit', CAST(0x0000A0E600DE7920 AS DateTime), N'Covered Topics:', N'<ul><li>Your responsibilities under the FACTA-Red Flag Guidelines as a Data Furnisher</li><li>NEW FACTA Section 312 - Compliance</li><li>Using E-OSCAR to view and respond to consumer disputes (ACDV Responses)</li><li>Using E-OSCAR to create and submit interim maintenance requests (AUDs) for previously reported trade-lines</li><li>Review the different guidelines for reporting to each of the National Credit Reporting Agencies; Equifax, Experian, Innovis, and Trans Union</li><li>Reporting your information monthly using the METRO or METRO-2 format</li><li>Reviewing your individual and joint tradeline information in order to be in compliance and reduce risk or class action</li></ul>', N'<p>The changes to FACTA will impact everyone in your institution dealing with consumers, credit information, and/or Identity Theft. This informative session is for Branch Managers, Assistant Branch Managers, Customer Service Reps, Lenders, Compliance Officers, Risk Officers, Collectors, and Trainers.</p>', CAST(2.00 AS Decimal(18, 2)), N'CreditDataEN1012.wmv', 10574, N'info@ttstrain.com', N'| ', CAST(0x0000A0B400B09AF0 AS DateTime), CAST(0x0000A0B400B2CD70 AS DateTime), NULL)
GO
INSERT [dbo].[Webinar] ([idWebinar], [Description], [DescriptionLong], [ImageUrl], [SmallImageUrl], [Status], [Title], [Date], [LearnCaption], [LearnBody], [WhoAttend], [Duration], [RecordingUrl], [idPresenter], [AdditionalNotifications], [ceu], [DateCreated], [DateChanged], [ConnectionInfo]) VALUES (1211, N'<p>This webinar will provide bankers with a clear understanding of Article 9''s key rules.</p>', N'<p>This webinar will provide bankers with a clear understanding of Article 9''s key rules.  We''ll include simple, straightforward information.</p>', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', 4, N'Secured Transactions', CAST(0x0000A0EE00DE7920 AS DateTime), N'Covered Topics:', N'<ul><li>Jointly-owned collateral</li><li>Lapse period</li><li>Debtor name</li><li>Termination</li><li>Priorities</li><li>Purchase-money situations</li><li>Information on securing and perfecting common types of collateral</li></ul>  <p>This webinar will include a colorful and easy-to-read handout that can be used for future reference, and bankers will particularly appreciate the quick-reference chart for common types of collateral.</p>', N'<p>Lenders, loan processors, compliance officers and loan review personnel will enjoy this webinar.</p>', CAST(2.00 AS Decimal(18, 2)), N'SecuredTransRB1012.wmv', 11158, N'info@ttstrain.com', N'| ', CAST(0x0000A0B700A36BF0 AS DateTime), CAST(0x0000A0B700A43EE0 AS DateTime), NULL)
GO
INSERT [dbo].[Webinar] ([idWebinar], [Description], [DescriptionLong], [ImageUrl], [SmallImageUrl], [Status], [Title], [Date], [LearnCaption], [LearnBody], [WhoAttend], [Duration], [RecordingUrl], [idPresenter], [AdditionalNotifications], [ceu], [DateCreated], [DateChanged], [ConnectionInfo]) VALUES (1213, N'<p>This one-hour webinar will help sales managers 
improve the focus of coaching as well as help your staff improve 
their skills.</p>', N'<p>Does your sales team have a problem with bloated pipelines filled with prospects that have been there for months? If so, there are probably a couple of reasons why. First, they aren''t prospecting enough so they are afraid to take prospects off the list. Second, they don''t have a good selling system for moving prospects from 1st to 2nd to home base. </p><p>This Coaching Pipeline Management webinar will help sales managers improve the focus of coaching as well as help your people improve their skills, their time management and their sales results utilizing a tool called the EPAS (Emergency Pipeline Action Steps).&nbsp; This disciplined process of evaluating your pipeline will also help you create a more predictable and valid pipeline so that you can forecast your sales more accurately.</p>', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', 4, N'Coaching Pipeline Management', CAST(0x0000A10E00E6B680 AS DateTime), N'Covered Topics:', N'<p>This one-hour sales management webinar will help sales managers develop the critical skills needed to:</p><ul><li>Coach your salespeople through a systematic pipeline review process to discover if a prospect is real or not</li><li>Introduce and utilize a proactive Effective Selling System to improve your sales staff''s ability to move qualified prospects more effectively through their pipeline</li><li>Make your pipeline a credible, predictive tool to forecast and grow your business</li></ul>', N'<p>Sales managers in all lines of business and trainers will all benefit by this webinar.</p>', CAST(1.00 AS Decimal(18, 2)), N'PipelineIW1112.wmv', 18308, N'info@ttstrain.com, sandy@cftncs.org', N'|<br>', CAST(0x0000A0BE00EB61D0 AS DateTime), CAST(0x0000A0BE00ECC160 AS DateTime), NULL)
GO
INSERT [dbo].[Webinar] ([idWebinar], [Description], [DescriptionLong], [ImageUrl], [SmallImageUrl], [Status], [Title], [Date], [LearnCaption], [LearnBody], [WhoAttend], [Duration], [RecordingUrl], [idPresenter], [AdditionalNotifications], [ceu], [DateCreated], [DateChanged], [ConnectionInfo]) VALUES (1214, N'<p>This two-hour webinar will walk you through the complicated process of dealing with a customer''s death, both on the deposit and loan side; as well as the unique issues of doing business with the decedent''s estate.</p>', N'<p>Ironically when a financial institution finds out that a deposit or loan customer has died, confusion and dread seem to be the normal reaction. This two-hour webinar will walk you through the complicated process of dealing with a customer''s death, both on the deposit and loan side; as well as the unique issues of doing business with the decedent''s estate. </p>', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', 4, N'What to Do When a Customer Dies', CAST(0x0000A10200A4CB80 AS DateTime), N'Topics of Discussion:', N'<ul>  <li>What documents are required upon the death of an individual?</li>  <li>What actions should the financial institution take on deposit accounts owned by the decedent?</li>  <li>How does the financial institution deal with the decedent''s estate?</li>  <li>What does the financial institution do if there is not an estate?</li>  <li>What happens if the decedent had a safe deposit box?</li>  <li>How should the financial institution handle "death" as a default on a loan?</li>  <li>What does every lender need to know about doing business with the borrower''s estate?</li>  <li>What steps can a financial institution take to protect its collateral after the borrower has died?</li>  <li>How does the financial institution handle issues of guarantors, setoff and insurance once the borrower has died?</li>  <li>How does the death of a key person affect the borrowings of Corporations, Partnerships, Limited Liability Companies, Trusts and other legal entities?</li></ul>', N'<p>New account representatives, personal bankers, CSR''s, lenders and loan operations will all find this seminar very beneficial.</p>', CAST(2.00 AS Decimal(18, 2)), N'CustomerDiesBU1112.wmv', 10609, N'info@ttstrain.com', N'2.5 CCSR and CPB credits. |The Institute of Certified Bankers TM (ICB) is dedicated to promoting the highest standards of performance and ethics within the financial services industry. This webinar has been approved for 2.5 CCSR and CPB credits. This statement should not be viewed as an endorsement of this program or its sponsor.', CAST(0x0000A0BE00FD8270 AS DateTime), CAST(0x0000A0BE00FE0F10 AS DateTime), NULL)
GO
INSERT [dbo].[Webinar] ([idWebinar], [Description], [DescriptionLong], [ImageUrl], [SmallImageUrl], [Status], [Title], [Date], [LearnCaption], [LearnBody], [WhoAttend], [Duration], [RecordingUrl], [idPresenter], [AdditionalNotifications], [ceu], [DateCreated], [DateChanged], [ConnectionInfo]) VALUES (1215, N'This webinar will address the grey areas regarding 
the Adverse Action Notices and the credit score disclosure requirements
 of the Dodd-Frank Act.', N'<p><b>Compliance ALERT</b> - Section 1100F Dodd-Frank Act</p><p>There seems to be some grey areas that need to be addressed regarding the Adverse Action Notices and the credit score disclosure requirements of the Dodd-Frank Act.&nbsp; This affects both <b>REG V</b> of the Fair Credit Reporting Act (FCRA) and <b>REG B</b> of the Equal Credit Opportunity Act (ECOA).</p><p>The Feds have added two new REG V Risk Base Pricing Notices and issued changes to REG B''s Adverse Action Notices, C1-C5!</p><p>Get some practical advice on how and when.&nbsp; Sign up for our webinar or get the OnDemand recording.</p>', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', 4, N'Reg V & B, Credit Scoring and the New Adverse Action Notice(s) Compliance Points', CAST(0x0000A10A00DE7920 AS DateTime), N'Covered Topics:', N'<ul><li>The new credit score disclosure requirements</li><li>What to do if you don’t use credit scores or no score is available!</li><li>When are the new Adverse Action Notices required?</li><li>Do these requirements compare to or replace the new risk-based pricing requirements?</li><li>AAN Rules for joint applicants</li><li>Using multiple credit scores and consumer disclosure</li><li>What you need to do if the credit score is not available</li><li>Account review(s) and consumer notifications</li><li>Rules regarding multi-party transactions</li><li>Examples and Model Notices</li></ul>', N'<p>This informative session is designed for Presidents, Managers, Credit Analysts, Commercial &amp; Consumer Lenders, Compliance &amp; Risk Officers, Human Resource Trainers, and anyone responsible for establishing, reviewing, &amp; maintaining policy &amp; procedures.</p>', CAST(2.00 AS Decimal(18, 2)), N'REGVBRD1112.wmv', 10574, N'info@ttstrain.com', N'| ', CAST(0x0000A0C200A325A0 AS DateTime), CAST(0x0000A0C200A48530 AS DateTime), NULL)
GO
INSERT [dbo].[Webinar] ([idWebinar], [Description], [DescriptionLong], [ImageUrl], [SmallImageUrl], [Status], [Title], [Date], [LearnCaption], [LearnBody], [WhoAttend], [Duration], [RecordingUrl], [idPresenter], [AdditionalNotifications], [ceu], [DateCreated], [DateChanged], [ConnectionInfo]) VALUES (1216, N'<p>In this webinar, Anne Lolley will summarize the nuts and bolts of the federal lending requirements.</p>', N'<p>In this webinar, Anne Lolley will summarize the nuts and bolts of the federal lending requirements.&nbsp; The discussed material will include information on:</p>', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', 4, N'Lending 101', CAST(0x0000A11700A4CB80 AS DateTime), N'Covered Topics:', N'<ul><li><i><b>Federal compliance rules.</b></i> Concise summaries of the rules on appraisals, BSA requirements, Reg AA, environmental rules, Reg B, FACTA, insurance disclosures, flood insurance, HMDA, homeownership counseling, LTV limits, privacy, RESPA, REG U, risk-based financing, service member requirements and Truth-in-Lending.</li><li><i><b>Supplemental Memos and Charts.</b></i>&nbsp; Detailed information on potential trouble spots will include:&nbsp; Right of rescission, adverse action, referral-fee checklist, refinancing and renewals, Reg O, appraisals and evaluations.</li><li><i><b>UCCC Rules.</b></i>&nbsp; A brief summary for states having this law.</li><li><i><b>Loan documentation.</b></i>&nbsp; Documentation for loans involving business entities, living trusts and powers of attorney.</li><li><i><b>Cites to the Actual Laws.</b></i>&nbsp; Will enable bankers locate the legal source of various requirements.</li><li><i><b>Detailed Index.</b></i>&nbsp; This invaluable tool will allow bankers locate information quickly.</li></ul>', N'<p>All the webinar information will be clearly documented in a 50+ page handbook filled with clear charts and cite references.&nbsp; We are confident that <i><b>lenders, loan processors and compliance officers</b></i> will be referring to this booklet time and time again.&nbsp; In addition, the webinar can be an invaluable training tool for <i><b>newer lenders and processors</b></i>.</p>', CAST(2.00 AS Decimal(18, 2)), N'Lending101FT1112.wmv', 11158, N'info@ttstrain.com', N'| ', CAST(0x0000A0C200DF4C10 AS DateTime), CAST(0x0000A0C200E0F1F0 AS DateTime), NULL)
GO
INSERT [dbo].[Webinar] ([idWebinar], [Description], [DescriptionLong], [ImageUrl], [SmallImageUrl], [Status], [Title], [Date], [LearnCaption], [LearnBody], [WhoAttend], [Duration], [RecordingUrl], [idPresenter], [AdditionalNotifications], [ceu], [DateCreated], [DateChanged], [ConnectionInfo]) VALUES (1217, N'<p>This webinar will provide knowledge in the wide variety of service businesses that exist and how 
those businesses should be analyzed from a financial standpoint.</p>', N'<p>This program will provide lenders and other credit professionals with knowledge in the wide variety of service businesses that exist and how those businesses should be analyzed from a financial standpoint.</p><p>Particular attention will be paid to the ways in which service businesses differ financially from one another depending upon their industry sector.&nbsp; Case studies of service businesses will be used to demonstrate the most effective ways of analyzing them and the types of borrowing needs that they have.&nbsp; At the conclusion of this program, attendees will know the right questions to ask of service businesses and be able to distinguish between low and high quality lending opportunities.</p>', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', 4, N'Analyzing Service Businesses', CAST(0x0000A10100DE7920 AS DateTime), N'Covered Topics:', N'<ul><li>Defining service businesses</li><li>The importance of service businesses in today''s economy</li><li>Cash drivers for service businesses</li><li>Questions to ask when analyzing credit requests from service businesses</li></ul>', N'<ul><li>Credit Analysts</li><li>Loan Officers</li><li>Branch Managers</li><li>Loan Committee members</li><li>Board Members</li><li>Business Development Officers</li></ul>', CAST(2.00 AS Decimal(18, 2)), N'ServiceRF1112.wmv', 27, N'info@ttstrain.com', N'|', CAST(0x0000A0C900F12660 AS DateTime), CAST(0x0000A0C900F2CC40 AS DateTime), NULL)
GO
INSERT [dbo].[Webinar] ([idWebinar], [Description], [DescriptionLong], [ImageUrl], [SmallImageUrl], [Status], [Title], [Date], [LearnCaption], [LearnBody], [WhoAttend], [Duration], [RecordingUrl], [idPresenter], [AdditionalNotifications], [ceu], [DateCreated], [DateChanged], [ConnectionInfo]) VALUES (1218, N'<p>By attending this program, lenders will gain a greater understanding and
 comfort level with the methodologies to employ when analyzing these 
types of borrowing requests.</p>', N'<p>Lenders are often asked to finance the purchase of an existing business by a new owner.&nbsp; Participating in this type of financing can be highly risky in some cases.&nbsp; The level of risk depends upon a number of factors, including the purchase price for the business, the value of the assets being purchased, and the future potential of the business to generate cashflow.&nbsp; This program will examine these issues as well as other important concepts such as non-compete agreements and the role of goodwill.&nbsp; By attending this program, lenders will gain a greater understanding and comfort level with the methodologies to employ when analyzing these types of borrowing requests.</p>', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', 4, N'Analyzing the Purchase of Existing Businesses', CAST(0x0000A11F00A4CB80 AS DateTime), N'Covered Topics:', N'<ul><li>Analyzing Historical Performance</li><li>Non-compete Agreements</li><li>Goodwill</li><li>Seller Financing</li><li>Asking the right questions</li></ul>', N'<ul><li>Credit Analysts</li><li>Loan Officers</li><li>Branch Managers</li><li>Loan Committee members</li><li>Board Members</li><li>Business Development Officers</li></ul>', CAST(2.00 AS Decimal(18, 2)), N'AnalyzingPurcBusPB1212.wmv', 27, N'info@ttstrain.com', N'|', CAST(0x0000A0C900F58B60 AS DateTime), CAST(0x0000A0C900F6A4A0 AS DateTime), NULL)
GO
INSERT [dbo].[Webinar] ([idWebinar], [Description], [DescriptionLong], [ImageUrl], [SmallImageUrl], [Status], [Title], [Date], [LearnCaption], [LearnBody], [WhoAttend], [Duration], [RecordingUrl], [idPresenter], [AdditionalNotifications], [ceu], [DateCreated], [DateChanged], [ConnectionInfo]) VALUES (1219, N'<p>What steps should your financial institution take to avoid some 
of the recent enforcement actions and violations cited for UDAP, BSA, 
Reg E and various compliance regulations.</p>', N'<p align="center"><b>HOT NEWS: UDAP VIOLATIONS ARE EXPENSIVE! </b></p><p align="center"><b>Could your financial institution be next?</b></p><p align="center"><b>PRESS RELEASE: September 24, 2012:</b></p><p align="left">The FDIC and the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau (CFPB) announced a joint public enforcement action with an order requiring Discover Bank to refund approximately <b>$200 million</b> to more than 3.5 million consumers and pay a <b>$14 million civil money penalty</b>. This action results from an investigation started by the FDIC which the CFPB joined last year. The joint investigation concerned deceptive telemarketing and sales tactics used by Discover to mislead consumers into paying for various credit card "add-on products" - payment protection, credit score tracking, identity theft protection, and wallet protection.&nbsp; Source: http://www.consumerfinance.gov/pressreleases/discover-consent-order/</p><p>All financial institutions use vendors for various aspects of providing products and services to their customers. They range from data processing, credit bureau reporting, telemarketing, loan servicing, ODP processing, and many other activities. A financial institution''s responsibility for third-party activity is the <b>SAME</b> as if it were being handled directly by the financial institution. UDAP (Unfair Deceptive Acts and Practices, and the UDAAP potential under Dodd-Frank for abusive acts) are being cited more frequently in enforcement actions, particularly with third-party services. Learn now to integrate third-party activities into your financial institution''s Compliance Management System.&nbsp; Effective third-party management programs incorporate:</p><blockquote><ol><li>Risk Assessment</li><li>Due Diligence</li><li>Contract Structuring and Review</li><li>Oversight</li></ol></blockquote><p>What steps should <u>your financial institution</u> take to avoid some of the recent enforcement actions and violations cited for UDAP, BSA, Reg E and various compliance regulations that involved inadequate due diligence and Board oversight for third-party activity?</p>', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', 4, N'Third Party Oversight and UDAP - Steps for Effective Vendor Management', CAST(0x0000A10800DE7920 AS DateTime), N'What You Will Learn:', N'<ul><li>What are the five types of risk in third party activities?</li><li>How can the risks be managed and mitigated? </li><li>What provisions should be included in your vendor contracts?</li><li>What areas should be reviewed in the third party provider''s policies, procedures, and internal controls? What about their training programs and complaint procedures?</li><li>What type of monitoring programs and internal controls should your financial institution incorporate to ensure compliance with Federal laws and regulatory guidance?</li><li>What are some of the current regulatory guidance references?</li><li>What are some "best practices" for third-party oversight, monitoring complaints, and anticipating UDAP issues?</li><li>What are some of the recent UDAP cases in third-party services?</li><li>BONUS - The materials include references to several regulatory publications and recent UDAP cases and enforcement actions</li></ul>', N'<p>This informative webinar is designed for senior management, risk managers, Board members, loan and deposit operation managers, compliance officers, and internal auditors.</p>', CAST(2.00 AS Decimal(18, 2)), N'VendorManagementYH1112.wmv', 14668, N'info@ttstrain.com', N'| ', CAST(0x0000A0D8010B3E10 AS DateTime), CAST(0x0000A0D8010DFD30 AS DateTime), NULL)
GO
INSERT [dbo].[Webinar] ([idWebinar], [Description], [DescriptionLong], [ImageUrl], [SmallImageUrl], [Status], [Title], [Date], [LearnCaption], [LearnBody], [WhoAttend], [Duration], [RecordingUrl], [idPresenter], [AdditionalNotifications], [ceu], [DateCreated], [DateChanged], [ConnectionInfo]) VALUES (1220, N'<p>The webinar focuses on the techniques and strategies you need in order to handle your job responsibilities successfully.</p>', N'<p>If you are a supervisor, if you need others to take direction from you in order to succeed, you will find this program of tremendous value.&nbsp; The webinar focuses on the techniques and strategies you need in order to handle your job responsibilities successfully, while at the same time, increasing your personal job satisfaction. </p><p>Supervisors must master the art of juggling - staff, schedules, meetings, compliance concerns, goals that must be met, deadlines that won''t wait, on-going training needs, serving as a back-up for the employee that didn''t come in...the list goes on and on. We''ll discuss how to keep all the balls in the air without breaking a sweat.<br></p><p>This program will ramp up your leadership skills and address critical supervisory issues necessary to becoming an excellent manager.&nbsp; If you are ready to take your commitment and skill set to the next level register today for this program, you will be eager to put to work what you''ve learned!</p><p align="center"><b>Join us, you''ll learn a positive, real-world approach to inspiring others to deliver extraordinary results.</b></p>', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', 4, N'The Four C''s of Exceptional Supervision - Conveying, Coaching, Correcting and Celebrating', CAST(0x0000A11600A4CB80 AS DateTime), N'What You Will Learn:', N'<ul><li>Creating a Quality Workplace</li><li>Building Trust, Respect and Confidence</li><li>Excelling at Effective Communication</li><li>Understanding the Supervisor''s Essential Role in all Aspects of Training</li><li>Supporting Change</li><li>Garnering Support at Every Level</li><li>Correcting and Addressing Behaviors and Choices that Don''t Work</li><li>Coaching - When and Why and How </li><li>Learning How to Handle - Complaining, Whining and Gossip </li><li>Providing Performance Feedback </li><li>Improving Work Habits</li><li>Resolving Conflict</li><li>Encouraging Your Staff to be Self-Managed</li></ul>', N'<p>Trainers, supervisors, assistant supervisors, or anyone with supervising responsibilities.</p>', CAST(2.00 AS Decimal(18, 2)), N'FourCBU1112.wmv', 25, N'info@ttstrain.com', N'| ', CAST(0x0000A0D8011494B0 AS DateTime), CAST(0x0000A0F900AFC800 AS DateTime), NULL)
GO
INSERT [dbo].[Webinar] ([idWebinar], [Description], [DescriptionLong], [ImageUrl], [SmallImageUrl], [Status], [Title], [Date], [LearnCaption], [LearnBody], [WhoAttend], [Duration], [RecordingUrl], [idPresenter], [AdditionalNotifications], [ceu], [DateCreated], [DateChanged], [ConnectionInfo]) VALUES (1221, N'<p>Vendor management is a hot topic for examinations today. </p>', N'<p>Vendor Management is a key element of your overall information security program as well as required by the FACTA ID Theft Red Flag program, Authentication in an Internet Banking Environment guidance, Risk Management of Remote Deposit Capture guidance, and most recently the FFIEC Cloud Computing Outsourcing informational paper.&nbsp; When you outsource, you are placing your confidential customer information in someone else''s hands along with the control for the security of that information, but you still retain the responsibility for ensuring the integrity, confidentiality, and security of the information.&nbsp; While you need to trust your third parties, the trust can’t be blind.&nbsp; The due diligence process is imperative prior to entering into a relationship.&nbsp; You need to establish rules and guidelines for a successful relationship and establish performance measurement criteria.&nbsp; Just as you run your business with best practices in mind your outsourced partners should do the same.&nbsp; The outsourcing environment is also under going some changes with the arrival of "cloud computing", which makes the due diligence process even more critical.&nbsp; But don''t forget about what happens after the contract is signed, due diligence is only part of the equation.&nbsp; Continuing to oversee and monitor that relationship and ensuring performance standards and security requirements are adhered to is also critical.&nbsp; Vendor management is a hot topic for examinations today. </p><p>In this presentation we will answer some key questions:</p><ul><li>How do you develop an effective measurement program and criteria?</li><li>Where do you start?</li><li>What are the risks with not having appropriate measurement tools?</li></ul>', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', 4, N'Vendor Management Program - An Enterprise-wide Focus', CAST(0x0000A12C00DE7920 AS DateTime), N'Learning Objectives:', N'<ul><li>Gain an understanding of what the vendor management program is and what it should address</li><li>Discover why you need a vendor management program</li><li>Gather information on the steps for performing vendor due diligence</li><li>Gather information on what should be addressed in the vendor risk assessment</li><li>Gather information on what is needed to effectively oversee the relationship</li></ul><p>Join Susan for a fast paced, information packed webinar on how to develop your vendor management program and be prepared for your next examination.</p>', N'<p>Senior Management, Information Security Officers, Compliance Officers, Risk Managers, IT Managers, Operations Managers.</p>', CAST(2.00 AS Decimal(18, 2)), N'VendorManagementJN1212.wmv', 10607, N'info@ttstrain.com', N'|', CAST(0x0000A0DF0116C730 AS DateTime), CAST(0x0000A0DF0118F9B0 AS DateTime), NULL)
GO
INSERT [dbo].[Webinar] ([idWebinar], [Description], [DescriptionLong], [ImageUrl], [SmallImageUrl], [Status], [Title], [Date], [LearnCaption], [LearnBody], [WhoAttend], [Duration], [RecordingUrl], [idPresenter], [AdditionalNotifications], [ceu], [DateCreated], [DateChanged], [ConnectionInfo]) VALUES (1222, N'<p>This session will review the ACH Rules changes that occurred in 2012 and highlight some of the changes coming for 2013.</p>', N'<p>Remaining in compliance with the ACH Operation Rules is a must! Each year, new rule amendments are implemented and it is vital that you are aware of these changes and take the steps within your organization to ensure compliance.&nbsp; This session will review the ACH Rules changes that occurred in 2012 and highlight some of the changes coming for 2013.</p>', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', 4, N'The ACH - A Look Back and A Look Ahead', CAST(0x0000A11D00A4CB80 AS DateTime), N'Covered Topics:', N'<ul><li>Minor Impact - Category C 2012 Rule Changes including:</li><ul><li>Clarification of Recurring TEL Authorization Retention Requirements</li><li>Correct to Payment Type Code for TEL Entries</li><li>Elimination of WEB Exposure Limits</li><li>Audit Changes</li></ul><li>IAT Changes that will take place in March of 2013</li><li>Return Reason Code R16 changes and more!</li></ul><p>As an added bonus, you''ll get updated on Expedited Processing and Settlement (EPS), Healthcare Rules and the ACH, The FFIEC updates and the new Consumer Financial Protection Bureau. </p>', N'<p>Operations, Compliance, Audit personnel.</p>', CAST(2.00 AS Decimal(18, 2)), N'ACH1212.wmv', 19383, N'info@ttstrain.com', N'2.4 AAP credits|This webinar is eligible for 2.4 Accredited ACH Professional Program credits.', CAST(0x0000A0E000B3A060 AS DateTime), CAST(0x0000A0E000B58C90 AS DateTime), NULL)
GO
INSERT [dbo].[Webinar] ([idWebinar], [Description], [DescriptionLong], [ImageUrl], [SmallImageUrl], [Status], [Title], [Date], [LearnCaption], [LearnBody], [WhoAttend], [Duration], [RecordingUrl], [idPresenter], [AdditionalNotifications], [ceu], [DateCreated], [DateChanged], [ConnectionInfo]) VALUES (1223, N'<p>Learn the safe way to handle checks and be sure that you and your 
financial institution can be protected from loss on the negotiable 
instruments.</p>', N'<p>Why do we make handling checks so hard?&nbsp; These simple do''s and don''ts will keep your financial institution from losing money and creating chaos in the back office.&nbsp; Checks are contracts and should be handled like any other legal document.&nbsp; There are reasons why we do not put business checks into personal accounts and why we do not give less cash on business accounts.&nbsp; Learn the safe way to handle checks and be sure that you and your financial institution can be protected from loss on the negotiable instruments.</p>', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', 4, N'Do''s and Don''ts of Checks:  How to Avoid Loss', CAST(0x0000A15500A4CB80 AS DateTime), N'What You Will Learn:', N'<ul><li>The simplest rule about checks that will save your financial institutions thousands of dollars</li><li>The connections between checks and account agreements-if you have not signed the signature card you cannot get the money</li><li>Postdated, stale dated, erasures, alterations and more lessons we need to learn</li><li>Why your institution needs to know about the negligence rule and the bank statement rule</li><li>Should we check endorsements and send them back as "missing"?</li><li>What should we do with checks for deceased people?<br></li><li>Treasury checks, postal money orders and other special checks</li><li>Why we absolutely do not give cash back, cash or deposit into personal accounts checks made payable to a business</li></ul>', N'<p>Tellers, Head Tellers, Cashiers, Managers, Branch Operations, Officers who okay checks and deposit representatives who work with checks and accounts</p>', CAST(2.00 AS Decimal(18, 2)), N'ChecksAW0113.wmv', 10568, N'info@ttstrain.com', N'2.5 CE Credits|After attending this webinar, each attendee can receive a certificate of attendance for CE Credits.', CAST(0x0000A0ED00AEAEC0 AS DateTime), CAST(0x0000A0ED00B54640 AS DateTime), NULL)
GO
INSERT [dbo].[Webinar] ([idWebinar], [Description], [DescriptionLong], [ImageUrl], [SmallImageUrl], [Status], [Title], [Date], [LearnCaption], [LearnBody], [WhoAttend], [Duration], [RecordingUrl], [idPresenter], [AdditionalNotifications], [ceu], [DateCreated], [DateChanged], [ConnectionInfo]) VALUES (1224, N'<p>In this line-by-line program, we will review the interesting changes in the new report and some of the challenges.</p>', N'<p>The countdown begins for implementation of the new Currency Transaction Report.&nbsp; In this line-by-line program, we will review the interesting changes in the new report and some of the challenges.&nbsp; You will receive a handbook with over 20 examples of how to complete the CTR for trusts, businesses, sole proprietors, multiple persons, aggregated transactions and so many more issues that occur in the daily operations of your financial institution.&nbsp; Beyond an introduction, this program will help you work with accountholders who own multiple businesses and personal accounts with ease.</p>', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', 4, N'Mastering the New Currency Transaction Report', CAST(0x0000A14000A4CB80 AS DateTime), N'What You Will Learn About the New Currency Transaction Report:', N'<ul><li>Line-by-line review of the report</li><li>How to name your report when more than one entity is involved</li><li>RSSD numbers by branch </li><li>What is a FinCEN directed backfiling?</li><li>Understand NAICS codes and occupation requirements</li><li>How to complete for multiple persons, joint accounts and unknown persons</li><li>How to complete when your accountholder has multiple businesses and personal accounts</li><li>How to complete when you have a trust, power of attorney or other fiduciary transaction</li><li>How to handle wires, prepaid access, checks cashed and other transactions</li></ul>', N'<p>All tellers, head tellers, CTR Coordinators, BSA Officers, Deposit Operations and any other area that deals with Currency Transaction Reports.</p>', CAST(2.00 AS Decimal(18, 2)), N'MasterNewCTRRT0113.wmv', 10568, N'info@ttstrain.com, ceskew@coloeast.com', N'2.5 CE Credits|After attending this webinar, each attendee can receive a certificate of attendance for CE Credits.', CAST(0x0000A0ED00B9F190 AS DateTime), CAST(0x0000A0ED00BB0AD0 AS DateTime), NULL)
GO
INSERT [dbo].[Webinar] ([idWebinar], [Description], [DescriptionLong], [ImageUrl], [SmallImageUrl], [Status], [Title], [Date], [LearnCaption], [LearnBody], [WhoAttend], [Duration], [RecordingUrl], [idPresenter], [AdditionalNotifications], [ceu], [DateCreated], [DateChanged], [ConnectionInfo]) VALUES (1225, N'<p>We''ll go in-depth on the details of the appraisal and valuation process, from both the lender and appraiser side of the game.</p>', N'<p>The past few years have seen significant developments in real estate appraisals and evaluation rule and regulations. Revised Interagency Guidelines and new rules under Reg. Z have been issued, and additional requirements have been proposed due to Dodd-Frank.</p><p>As breakdowns in appraisal practices have been partly blamed for the mortgage crisis, regulators have raised their expectations; lenders'' appraisal and evaluation programs must include more elements than ever before. Some of the themes being emphasized by the agencies are independence of the appraiser and evaluator, reviews, and qualifications.</p><p>There are also restrictions against using AVMs (automated valuation models), BPOs (broker price opinions), and tax valuations that has upset many in the industry.</p><p>Do you know the requirements? We''ll go in-depth on the details of the appraisal and valuation process, from both the lender and appraiser side of the game, to provide a thorough understanding of what is required and what you have to have.</p>', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', 4, N'Dealing with Appraisals:  Compliance with New Standards', CAST(0x0000A11800DE7920 AS DateTime), N'Covered Topics:', N'<ul><li>Regulations and Interagency Guidelines - requirements for lenders and brokers</li><li>Clarified independence requirements and the importance of this to examiners</li><li>The many forms of appraisals and evaluations - what can you use and when? AVMs and BPOs aren''t what they used to be</li><li>Can we accept a previous appraisal? Dealing with "readdressed" and "transferred" appraisals</li><li>USPAP rules and standards - how do appraiser rules influence what lenders must do?</li><li>Dodd-Frank developments and coming changes to Regs. Z and B, including those for "higher-risk loans"</li><li>How to achieve appraiser independence - you''ve got to prove it</li><li>Anti-coercion and undue influence provisions of Reg Z - what can you NOT do (or say)?</li><li>Changes mandated for Fannie and Freddie lenders</li></ul>', N'<p>Real estate lenders, compliance officers, auditors, underwriters, appraisers (in-house or external), closing agents, management, and anyone else involved in the real estate or residential lending process with a need to understand the current state of appraisal regulation and requirements.</p><p><span style="font-style: italic;">Carl is an excellent speaker. If you have additional questions, he always follows up! - Brenda P., Northampton Cooperative Bank</span><br></p>', CAST(2.00 AS Decimal(18, 2)), N'AppraisalsLS1112.wmv', 24, N'info@ttstrain.com, rcapobianco@nsbonline.com, flipa@bellbanks.com', N'2.5 CLBB &amp; CRCM credits|The Institute of Certified Bankers (ICB) is dedicated to promoting the highest standards of performance and ethics within the financial services industry.&nbsp; The Are You Accepting Proper Appraisals? New Regulator Attention to the Requirements has been approved for 2.50 CLBB, 2.50 CRCM credits.&nbsp; This statement should not be viewed as an endorsement of this program or its sponsor.', CAST(0x0000A0F200B6A5D0 AS DateTime), CAST(0x0000A0F200B80560 AS DateTime), NULL)
GO
INSERT [dbo].[Webinar] ([idWebinar], [Description], [DescriptionLong], [ImageUrl], [SmallImageUrl], [Status], [Title], [Date], [LearnCaption], [LearnBody], [WhoAttend], [Duration], [RecordingUrl], [idPresenter], [AdditionalNotifications], [ceu], [DateCreated], [DateChanged], [ConnectionInfo]) VALUES (1226, N'<p>Critical compliance concerns right now; plus how to understand and deal with impending changes.</p>', N'<p><b>Critical compliance concerns right now; plus how to understand and deal with impending changes.</b></p><p>Mortgage lending is just about the most complicated compliance topic going these days. What are the examiners concerned with right now? When will the impending changes be effective? And how should you prioritize?</p><p>Answers to these questions are what we need to implement all of what''s coming. That''s what we''re going to talk about in this webinar; not the legalese of the statute, but what the CFPB and other agencies are saying about what their plans are for new regulation. We will answer the basic operational questions: what will we have to do, when will we have to do it, and what will it look like? The flood of information is already coming from the Bureau, and they''re under some pretty aggressive timelines. They may not meet all of them, but it won''t be from lack of trying.</p>', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', 4, N'Mortgage Lending Now and in the Near Future: Reg Z, RESPA and CFPB ', CAST(0x0000A12D00DE7920 AS DateTime), N'Covered Topics Include:', N'<ul><li>Final amendments to Reg. Z and RESPA soon to be announced - new disclosures, accompanying rules, including big changes to the APR calculations and record retention</li><li>Will we finally have resolution to what a "Qualified Mortgage" is? Will it be a legal safe harbor or a rebuttable presumption (and why does this matter)?</li><li>How about "Qualified Residential Mortgage" (QRM) rules? Note this is different from a Qualified Mortgage</li><li>Developments in loan originator compensation</li><li>New escrow rules</li><li>Clarity coming on ability-to-repay rules</li><li>When will the new HMDA data elements need to be collected and submitted?</li><li>Foreclosure activity: the $26 billion settlement, what that also means to all banks, and the CFPB''s servicing proposal - taming the Wild West</li><li>Treatment of servicemembers</li></ul><p>We''ll talk about all these and more, plus leave some time for Q&amp;A. Listen in to keep up to date with what is new and exciting in the world of mortgage compliance so you won’t miss anything.</p>', N'<p>Compliance officers, bank counsel, credit officers, loan officers, loss mitigation and asset management personnel, collectors, underwriters, senior management, and anyone else at your bank who has a hand in your residential mortgage operations.</p>', CAST(2.00 AS Decimal(18, 2)), N'MortgageLendingRN1212.wmv', 24, N'info@ttstrain.com', N'2.5 CPB, 2.5 CRCM credits|The Institute of Certified Bankers (ICB) is dedicated to promoting the highest standards of performance and ethics within the financial services industry.&nbsp; This webinar has been approved for 2.5 CPB, 2.5 CRCM credits.&nbsp; This statement should not be viewed as an endorsement of this program or its sponsor.', CAST(0x0000A0F200C1A250 AS DateTime), CAST(0x0000A122012BA6F0 AS DateTime), NULL)
GO
INSERT [dbo].[Webinar] ([idWebinar], [Description], [DescriptionLong], [ImageUrl], [SmallImageUrl], [Status], [Title], [Date], [LearnCaption], [LearnBody], [WhoAttend], [Duration], [RecordingUrl], [idPresenter], [AdditionalNotifications], [ceu], [DateCreated], [DateChanged], [ConnectionInfo]) VALUES (1227, N'How to Prepare and Manage the Risk', N'<p><b>How to Prepare and Manage the Risk</b></p><p>"UDAAP" could become the most significant term ever to affect bank compliance. That sounds pretty bold, but consider that the CFPB has been given an almost-unlimited mandate under Dodd-Frank to "take any action...to prevent a covered person or service provider from committing or engaging in an unfair, deceptive, or abusive act or practice under Federal law in connection with any transaction with a consumer for a consumer financial product or service, or the offering of a consumer financial product or service."</p><p>Although the UDAAP standard seems new, we''ve actually been familiar with "UDAP" (just one ''A'') for quite some time. That extra ''A'', for ''Abusive'', adds a new standard, however, and the CFPB is already active with enforcement actions (3 and counting so far).</p><p>What does all this mean to banks and the industry? At the very minimum, it means you must be familiar with what this new standard means for compliance and the risk management process. The rules of the game have changed, and technical compliance is no longer the only issue.</p><p>It means understanding what examiners are likely to focus on, including areas where a clear rule or regulation might not even apply. It''s a cultural shift in the regulatory function, and in this webinar we''ll discuss the meaning of UDAAP and how it will impact your bank.</p>', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', 4, N'The State of UDAAP: Dealing with a New Reality', CAST(0x0000A12500A4CB80 AS DateTime), N'Covered Topics:', N'<ul><li>UDAP vs. UDAAP: what does the introduction of "abusive" really do?</li><li>This isn''t only a CFPB issues - it will affect ALL banks, regardless of regulator</li><li>"Abusive" standards: how will this be enforced?</li><li>Scope of UDAAP: products, services, delivery channels and methods</li><li>UDAAP examples: where should your focus be?</li><li>Emphasis on sales and marketing practices, and product management</li><li>Cultural change brought by UDAAP</li><li>What are the agencies looking for?</li><li>Areas where you wouldn''t even think to look</li><li>How to prepare your UDAAP program</li><li>What are the regulatory expectations? Evaluations, risk assessments, more?</li><li>Going beyond the program: changing the focus of your organization</li></ul>', N'<p>UDAAP is an issue that affects most everyone in the financial institution. But in particular, compliance officers, auditors, management, counsel, marketing, sales, product development, business line management, and anyone else involved in any products, services, or practices that impact consumers will get valuable information from this webinar.</p>', CAST(2.00 AS Decimal(18, 2)), N'UDAAP1212.wmv', 24, N'info@ttstrain.com', N'2.5 CFMP &amp; CRCM Credits|The Institute of Certified Bankers (ICB) is dedicated to promoting the highest standards of performance and ethics within the financial services industry. This webinar has been approved for 2.5 CFMP &amp; CRCM credits. This statement should not be viewed as an endorsement of this program or its sponsor.', CAST(0x0000A0F200C57AB0 AS DateTime), CAST(0x0000A0F200C88020 AS DateTime), NULL)
GO
INSERT [dbo].[Webinar] ([idWebinar], [Description], [DescriptionLong], [ImageUrl], [SmallImageUrl], [Status], [Title], [Date], [LearnCaption], [LearnBody], [WhoAttend], [Duration], [RecordingUrl], [idPresenter], [AdditionalNotifications], [ceu], [DateCreated], [DateChanged], [ConnectionInfo]) VALUES (1228, N'<p>It''s that time of the year again when thoughts turn to IRS reporting issues and the myriad rules to follow and forms to complete.</p>', N'<p>It''s that time of the year again when thoughts turn to IRS reporting issues and the myriad rules to follow and forms to complete. This webinar deals with the many forms financial institutions must report, with an emphasis on when and exactly what to report. Easy-to-follow charts are included to complete each form. </p>', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', 4, N'IRS Information Reporting: What You Need to Know About the Rules and Forms', CAST(0x0000A12C00A4CB80 AS DateTime), N'Here is a sampling of what will be discussed:', N'<ul><li>Taxpayer Identification Numbers - soliciting them, reporting issues, mismatches from the IRS and what to do</li><li>Backup withholding - "B" notices: what to do and when</li><li>1099 reporting - its many and various forms, from interest and dividend income, abandoned and foreclosed property, IRA distributions, debt cancellation, and miscellaneous reporting</li><li>1098s - what amount is reportable here? How about points? What is a qualifying mortgage?</li><li>IRA reporting - 5498s and the 1099-R</li><li>Timing requirements for the various forms</li><li>Penalties for noncompliance and failure to file</li><li>Changes in reporting requirements for tax year 2011</li><li>Proposed new interest reporting requirements for nonresident alien customers </li><li>And much more</li></ul><p>Plus frequent question and answer sessions throughout this presentation.</p>', N'<p>Anyone in the institution having responsibilities to collect tax information, file the various forms the IRS requires, or someone who must be aware of the TIN requirements. This may include members of senior management, operations personnel, back-room personnel, as well as compliance officers, auditors, and attorneys, and anyone else in the institution that might benefit from this valuable information.</p>', CAST(2.00 AS Decimal(18, 2)), N'IRSInfoReptRS1212.wmv', 24, N'info@ttstrain.com', N'2.5 CRCM credits|The Institute of Certified Bankers (ICB) is dedicated to promoting the highest standards of performance and ethics within the financial services industry. This webinar has been approved for 2.5 CRCM credits.', CAST(0x0000A0F200E9BBF0 AS DateTime), CAST(0x0000A0F200EA4890 AS DateTime), NULL)
GO
INSERT [dbo].[Webinar] ([idWebinar], [Description], [DescriptionLong], [ImageUrl], [SmallImageUrl], [Status], [Title], [Date], [LearnCaption], [LearnBody], [WhoAttend], [Duration], [RecordingUrl], [idPresenter], [AdditionalNotifications], [ceu], [DateCreated], [DateChanged], [ConnectionInfo]) VALUES (1229, N'<p>This program provides a broad overview to the documentation process.</p>', N'<p>This webinar has been designed to provide commercial loan processors and junior commercial loan officers a broad introduction to the various documents needed in secure loan transactions.&nbsp; This seminar examines and explains the importance of proper documentation in the context of commercial lending.&nbsp; The goal of the program is to provide exposure to the specific documents needed to prefect and secure various commercial transactions.&nbsp; Specific case examples will be used for loan transactions covering various collateral types and loan types.</p>', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', 4, N'Introduction to Commercial Loan Documentation', CAST(0x0000A11F00DE7920 AS DateTime), N'Covered Topics:', N'<ul><li>Understanding the lien process</li><li>Three events of attachment</li><li>Lien perfection</li><li>The importance of liens from a collateral standpoint</li><li>Basic types of credit facilities</li><li>Types of Borrowers and the importance of understanding the differences</li><li>Types of Collateral</li><li>Where to search UCC 11</li><li>Where to file UCC</li><li>Using the information from the Secretary of State</li><li>ECOA Reg B Compliance - consistency in the process</li><li>Article 9 - UCC</li><li>Common problems in loan documentation</li></ul>', N'<p>This webinar is intended for commercial lenders, junior lenders, processors, and loan review staff or anyone else involved with commercial loans.</p>', CAST(2.00 AS Decimal(18, 2)), N'LoanDocXH1212.wmv', 10565, N'info@ttstrain.com', N'2.5 CE Credits|After attending this webinar, each attendee can receive a certificate of attendance for CE credits.', CAST(0x0000A0FA011148F0 AS DateTime), CAST(0x0000A0FA01285B30 AS DateTime), NULL)
GO
INSERT [dbo].[Webinar] ([idWebinar], [Description], [DescriptionLong], [ImageUrl], [SmallImageUrl], [Status], [Title], [Date], [LearnCaption], [LearnBody], [WhoAttend], [Duration], [RecordingUrl], [idPresenter], [AdditionalNotifications], [ceu], [DateCreated], [DateChanged], [ConnectionInfo]) VALUES (1230, N'<p>Tick, tock the Regulation E Subpart B clock is ticking.&nbsp; Are you ready?</p>', N'<p>The countdown to implement Regulation E governing consumer foreign remittances has begun and the CFPB has just announced <b>three new changes</b>.&nbsp; This program moves past definitions into the operations side of the regulation.&nbsp; You will receive checklists, sample policy, procedures, forms and other helpful tools to get your ready as the countdown begins.&nbsp; We will look at areas that may cause issues during the examination process on consumer foreign remittances and what you may do to be prepared.&nbsp; Tick, tock the Regulation E Subpart B clock is ticking.&nbsp; Are you ready?</p>', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', 4, N'Countdown to Regulation E Foreign Remittances:  Policy, Procedures, Logs, and More', CAST(0x0000A14300A4CB80 AS DateTime), N'What You Will Learn:', N'<ul><li>Key components that need to be in your Regulation E Policy whether you are in or you are out</li><li>Developing and designing an error resolution log</li><li>Procedures for cancellation and procedures for error resolution </li><li>What tools to use to develop estimates</li><li>Documenting your cancellations</li><li>What to do when your financial institution transitions from 100 or under to More than 100</li><li>How to fly under the radar and stay out of the Regulation E game</li><li>You will receive sample policy, procedures, and worksheets to begin your policy process</li><li>What to look for in your examination process</li></ul>', N'<p>Compliance officers, deposit operations personnel, Regulation E staff and persons who will be involved in the error resolution process.</p>', CAST(2.00 AS Decimal(18, 2)), N'RegEBT0113.wmv', 10568, N'info@ttstrain.com', N'2.5 CE Credits|After attending this webinar, each attendee can receive a certificate of attendance for CE Credits.', CAST(0x0000A10900BB9770 AS DateTime), CAST(0x0000A10900BD3D50 AS DateTime), NULL)
GO
INSERT [dbo].[Webinar] ([idWebinar], [Description], [DescriptionLong], [ImageUrl], [SmallImageUrl], [Status], [Title], [Date], [LearnCaption], [LearnBody], [WhoAttend], [Duration], [RecordingUrl], [idPresenter], [AdditionalNotifications], [ceu], [DateCreated], [DateChanged], [ConnectionInfo]) VALUES (1231, N'<p>If you want to know the latest and greatest IRA changes, this annual update is a "must" attend.</p>', N'<p>The year 2012 was an election year.&nbsp; There were many bills buried in Congress regarding IRAs that were not discussed or voted on due to provisions being tied to the Tax Cut Extension? or Expiration? Acts.&nbsp; If anything passes before the end of the year, these topics will be discussed in this two hour informative IRA Update.</p>', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', 4, N'IRA Update - What''s New for the Filing Season?', CAST(0x0000A14700A4CB80 AS DateTime), N'What You Will Learn:', N'<ul><li>What are the 2013 contribution limits and cost of living adjustments for Traditional, Roth and SEP IRAs?</li><li>What is the difference between a Traditional to Roth "conversion" and a QP to Roth "rollover"?</li><li>Have the Qualified Charitable Distribution provisions been reinstated?</li><li>Who is responsible for the deceased owner''s RMD in the year of death?</li><li>What are the primary steps to handle beneficiary payouts?</li><li>What are the most common IRS reporting errors regarding IRA distributions and contributions?</li></ul><p>This interactive session will allow time to answer your questions regarding IRA issues you encounter on a regular basis.</p>', N'<p>IRA personnel in New Accounts, CDs, Trust, Investments and Savings Departments who are involved with the opening, selling, and administration of IRA accounts will benefit greatly from the review of the more complicated aspects of the IRA. This is considered an "Intermediate" workshop.</p>', CAST(2.00 AS Decimal(18, 2)), N'IRAUpDateDP0113.wmv', 28, N'info@ttstrain.com, kbennett@ttstrain.com', N'2.5 CISP, 2.5 CRSP, 2.5 CTFA-FP credits|The Institute of Certified Bankers (ICB) is dedicated to promoting the highest standards of performance and ethics within the financial services industry.  IRA Update has been approved for 2.5 CISP, 2.5 CRSP, 2.5 CTFA credits.  CTFA credits should be distributed as follows: 2.5 FP.  This statement should not be viewed as an endorsement of this program or its sponsor.', CAST(0x0000A10900C08910 AS DateTime), CAST(0x0000A10900C34830 AS DateTime), NULL)
GO
INSERT [dbo].[Webinar] ([idWebinar], [Description], [DescriptionLong], [ImageUrl], [SmallImageUrl], [Status], [Title], [Date], [LearnCaption], [LearnBody], [WhoAttend], [Duration], [RecordingUrl], [idPresenter], [AdditionalNotifications], [ceu], [DateCreated], [DateChanged], [ConnectionInfo]) VALUES (1236, N'<p>A monthly webinar series to help you keep up with changes and deadlines in the compliance area. </p>', N'<p><b>Keeping up with changes and deadlines in the compliance area</b> gets more complex every year. Now, we can assist you with that task.</p>
<p><b><i>Carl Pry</i></b>, a well known and highly respected compliance expert will be presenting a monthly one-hour compliance update that will address <u>new items to be aware of, deadlines and what''s on the horizon</u>. In a simple language webinar format that you can view from your office, Carl will make sure you have the information you need to keep your financial institution in compliance.</p>
<h2>Features:</h2>
<ul>
<li>Monthly hot topics 
</li><li>Current deadlines 
</li><li>Upcoming regulations 
</li><li>Examiner guidance 
</li><li>Concise one hour format 
</li><li>Unlimited participants 
</li><li>One-low cost 
</li><li>Archived recording</li></ul>
<p>For only $159 per month with a six month commitment, you receive the live session and a link to the archived recording. Watch the live session or access the recording for the next 30 days. Imagine what you can save in reduced compliance violations or unnecessary research time.</p>', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', N'http://bankwebinars.com/content/images/bg.jpg', 2, N'Compliance Perspectives:  A Monthly Update', CAST(0x0000A38C00D63BC0 AS DateTime), N' ', N'&nbsp;', N'<p>Anyone in the institution having compliance responsibilities - when you think about this, it could be just about anyone in the institution. This may include members of senior management, operations personnel, lending personnel, underwriters, customer service representatives, back-room personnel, and of course compliance officers, auditors, and attorneys, and anyone else in the institution that might benefit from this valuable information.</p>', CAST(1.00 AS Decimal(18, 2)), N'', 24, N'info@ttstrain.com', N'1.25 CRCM Credits|The Institute of Certified Bankers (ICB) is dedicated to promoting the highest standards of performance and ethics within the financial services industry. This webinar has been approved for 1.25 CRCM credits. This statement should not be viewed as an endorsement of this program or its sponsor.', CAST(0x0000A109011753D0 AS DateTime), CAST(0x0000A27B00B4FFF0 AS DateTime), NULL)
GO
